Across 5 seeds: 15 player confrontations, contested lane held at the end of 5/5, net territory +0.
The bot TAKES ITS OBJECTIVE in most seeds and still ends with no net territory: it wins the war it started and loses ground elsewhere while committed. So militarism is not failing to achieve anything — it is paying for a won objective with what it cannot defend meanwhile. Raising conquest yields would not address that; the cost is the opportunity cost of commitment.</StdOut>
